  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking compared with 10.1.0 (10.2.0 is a minor version under the .NET-major versioning convention; pin an exact version). Depends on ApiFeatures.Authentications.Users.Cores (>= 10.0.0). The constants (AuthenticationProviders, UserStatuses, ValidationConstraints, BusinessMessageCodes, ValidationMessageCodes) and IUser, UserDto, Coordinate, CentralCoordinate moved to ApiFeatures.Authentications.Users.Cores (namespaces ApiFeatures.Authentications.Users.Cores.Constants / .Models). ValidRoles and UserPermissions were removed. UserDto gains Role (id, code, displayName) and Permissions (joined paths as granted, for example \"*\", \"user.*\"); UserDto.Roles now holds the role code (for example ADMIN, was free text such as admin) and UserDto.AssignedFeatures the same joined paths as Permissions; both are deprecated. Consumers must match wildcards segment-safely (see the Users.Cores README). Unchanged: the messages and the request client keep their namespaces and names, and the RabbitMQ message names are the same.",
